WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.369
-Our next guest is an Emmy-
and Tony Award-winning actor

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:05.371
you know from his work on "Monk"
and "The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel."

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:08.441
He stars in "Mr. Monk's
Last Case: A Monk Movie,"

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.577
which premieres
December 8th on Peacock.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:11.711
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:14.546
-We hired you to write
about your career

00:00:14.546 --> 00:00:16.582
as a police detective.

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:21.420
You solved 140 homicides.
That's the story we paid for.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.957
Not this.
Oh, here in Chapter 4,

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:29.262
you have two paragraphs
about the suspect

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:36.502
and seven, eight, nine pages
about his vacuum cleaner.

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:39.472
-We had the same vacuum cleaner,
the exact same model.

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:40.907
What are the odds of that?

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:45.311
-Please welcome back to the show
our friend Tony Shalhoub!

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:47.614
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:11.404
Welcome back!

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:12.672
-Thank you. Wow.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.574
It's been a while,
but it's great to be here.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:17.810
-It's great to have you here.
I was very happy to see you.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:18.845
You are a
Green Bay Packers fan.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:19.979
-Oh, indeed.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.480
-There was a
Sunday Night Football game.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.617
-Yes, against the
Kansas City Swifts -- Chiefs.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:25.885
-The Kansas City Swifts.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:28.354
Well, I was going to say,
you were on the sidelines.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:29.622
-There I am, yeah.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:31.324
-And it must have been
a rare case

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:34.160
where nobody cared
about you at all.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.794
-It was.

00:01:35.794 --> 00:01:39.732
It was -- My thunder
was not only stolen

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:42.302
but actually sent out
into the stratosphere.

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:43.803
Yeah.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:45.404
-Also, I want to note,
she's always in, like,

00:01:45.404 --> 00:01:48.607
a very warm box seat,
and you're just on the field.

00:01:48.607 --> 00:01:49.676
-No, no.
[ Laughs ]

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:53.712
No, actually,
that was just a pre-game.

00:01:53.712 --> 00:01:56.648
-Oh, oh.
-I actually was in a box, too.

00:01:56.648 --> 00:01:57.683
Do you know what's funny?

00:01:57.683 --> 00:01:59.953
Everyone, you know, asked me,

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.987
"Are you going to see
Taylor Swift?

00:02:01.987 --> 00:02:03.322
Did you see Taylor?"

00:02:03.322 --> 00:02:06.458
As if, like, there's one box,
you know, in the stadium.

00:02:06.458 --> 00:02:08.528
You know,
and I was really disa--

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:12.465
I was disappointed I didn't,
because she is --

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:15.668
I mean, she is such
an enormous "Monk" fan.

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:17.036
-Yeah.
-You know what I mean?

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:19.638
-Everybody knows that, yeah.
That would have been huge.

00:02:19.638 --> 00:02:20.940
-It would have been great,
so great for her.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:25.144
-I think I've heard her say
almost half her songs

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:26.946
are actually about "Monk."

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:29.048
-Subliminally, yes.

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:32.385
-You like watching football,
but you also like

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:33.852
not just what's happening
on the field.

00:02:33.852 --> 00:02:35.455
You're kind of obsessed
with what the coaches

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:36.689
are doing on the sidelines.

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:38.424
-Yeah, you know, I have this --
I love games.

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:40.526
You know, of course,
I'm obsessed with the Packers.

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:41.660
I'm from Green Bay.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:44.163
But, you know,
and I watch other games.

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:48.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
Hey, somebody from Green Bay.

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:49.869
-That -- By the way,
I've been to Green Bay.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:52.238
That might be half of them.
-Yeah.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:55.975
Yeah. Yeah, but there's just
a few things

00:02:55.975 --> 00:03:00.580
about it's televised,
watching games on TV.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.548
I mean, being there
live is fantastic,

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:05.651
but on TV, there's just one --

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:08.254
There's one thing
that really drives me insane.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:10.323
You know, when the cameras
are, you know,

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:13.125
panning the sideline,
and then, you know,

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:14.160
they -- Do you mind?

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.161
-Yeah.

00:03:16.161 --> 00:03:17.563
-They go, they shoot the coach,

00:03:17.563 --> 00:03:18.831
and the coach is,
like, doing this.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.432
It's like...

00:03:20.432 --> 00:03:21.701
-Yeah, he holds, like, a
clipboard in front of his face.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.802
-Yeah, what is that?
-Yeah.

00:03:23.802 --> 00:03:25.772
-This is -- What is that?

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:26.839
-It's like the
"Home Alone neighbor.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.674
Not the "Home Alone."
What is it?

00:03:28.674 --> 00:03:29.976
"Home Improvement."
-Yeah.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:32.344
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.344 --> 00:03:34.614
-Yeah, I don't know.
I don't know.

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:36.649
I mean, you know,
God bless the coaches.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.183
They got to do
what they got to do,

00:03:38.183 --> 00:03:41.754
but let's just move the camera
somewhere else, you know?

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.923
-If you want to show us their
mouth, we'll put them on TV,

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:45.157
but, otherwise,
we don't want to look at it.

00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:48.360
-Yeah. Or maybe they --
coaches could just get --

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:49.696
You know,
they have these headsets.

00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:52.031
Couldn't they just get
a little round disc

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:54.400
on the end of the mic,
so they can just talk and --

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.936
-Yeah, just say what they want.
You're right. The disc.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:04:00.138
Why aren't they doing the disc?
That's bad. Yeah, you're right.

00:04:00.138 --> 00:04:01.841
This is very exciting.

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:05.010
This is 14 years
since "Monk" ended,

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.079
and it ended well --
eight wonderful seasons.

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:09.582
You were very happy
with how it resolved itself.

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:11.817
-Yeah, we had a two-part finale.

00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:13.553
You know, we really
were proud of that.

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:16.122
It was -- You know, we --
Monk solves the case

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:18.157
of his wife's murder, finally.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:20.526
And the ratings
were really good.

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:22.628
And so, you know,
there wasn't a big incentive

00:04:22.628 --> 00:04:25.464
to revisit this character.

00:04:25.464 --> 00:04:27.533
And then -- Well, then
the pandemic happened,

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:30.903
and we did this public-service
announcement for Peacock,

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:33.305
and, you know,
talking about being safe

00:04:33.305 --> 00:04:35.140
and wearing masks
and all that.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.543
And, all of a sudden,
the response

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:40.279
to that public-service
announcement was huge.

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:42.148
And then we -- the writers
and the network said,

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:45.718
"Hey, let's try a 'Monk' movie."

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:48.154
-I mean, it's weird
and also fitting

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:49.555
that the pandemic
sort of brought it about,

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:52.792
because, of course, Monk
was this character with OCD,

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:54.060
a character with high anxiety.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:57.229
And we sort of all became
more like Monk.

00:04:57.229 --> 00:04:58.298
-Right.

00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:00.532
-For basically two years,
we all sort of

00:05:00.532 --> 00:05:01.867
Monked out a little bit.

00:05:01.867 --> 00:05:03.969
-Yeah. And that's kind of
what the --

00:05:03.969 --> 00:05:08.107
That's sort of laced into
the plot of our movie, you know,

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:12.878
the fact that he has gotten
knocked back on his heels way,

00:05:12.878 --> 00:05:16.182
way -- He's regressed.

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:19.519
He's now worse than he was when
we first met him, in the pilot.

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:21.721
And -- But also that
the world has changed,

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:24.590
and he doesn't look quite
so neurotic anymore.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:25.824
-Oh, well, that's good.

00:05:25.824 --> 00:05:27.559
Yeah, so he's worse,
but so are the rest of us.

00:05:27.559 --> 00:05:29.595
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:33.198
Your beautiful, talented wife,
Brooke, was the editor

00:05:33.198 --> 00:05:34.566
in the clip we showed.

00:05:34.566 --> 00:05:36.435
And --
-Yeah, she's the publisher.

00:05:36.435 --> 00:05:38.137
-The publisher. Excuse me.
-Yes.

00:05:38.137 --> 00:05:39.905
-But she's also --
I was not aware

00:05:39.905 --> 00:05:42.108
she has been
on "Monk" multiple times,

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:43.242
but as multiple
different characters.

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:44.710
-Yes. Never played
the same character twice.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:47.646
-This shows
Brooke's incredible range.

00:05:47.646 --> 00:05:49.848
Here she was there.
-Oh, the crazy cat lady.

00:05:49.848 --> 00:05:51.217
-Yep. I was going to say.

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:52.852
If you had asked me to guess
the name of the character,

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:54.152
I would have said that.

00:05:54.152 --> 00:05:55.921
Also did
some law-enforcement work.

00:05:55.921 --> 00:05:57.122
-Right.

00:05:57.122 --> 00:05:59.058
-Here she is --
Here's the clip we just saw

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:00.593
of her as the publisher.

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:02.862
-Right.
-Who was she here?

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:04.630
-Oh, this was one of
the roles --

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.465
She did a very dramatic role

00:06:06.465 --> 00:06:09.234
where a son of hers
is kidnapped or something, and
--

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:10.369
I can't remember the plot.

00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:12.337
And -- Sorry.

00:06:12.337 --> 00:06:15.274
And, yeah, it's a very, very
moving and a dramatic role.

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:18.244
-And then here she is as
a flight attendant.

00:06:18.244 --> 00:06:19.445
Excuse me.
-Yeah, a flight attendant.

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:22.314
Right. She plays this stewardess
who has been

00:06:22.314 --> 00:06:24.483
sober for many years, and then,
by the end of the flight,

00:06:24.483 --> 00:06:26.819
she's drinking out
of the little bottle.

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:28.287
-It really is.
She's a jack-of-all-trades.

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:29.421
-Yeah.
-It's very impressive.

00:06:29.421 --> 00:06:31.256
-She's the transforming actor.

00:06:31.256 --> 00:06:34.326
-I have more to ask about her
and more to ask about you.

00:06:34.326 --> 00:06:35.895
We're going to be right back
with Tony after this.

